{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And behold, the sound of the whip comes upon her</b> — to spur on the horse. But the correct interpretation in my eyes: 'whip' — to strike, a kind that produces a sound, which the Philistines make, like our tanbur, which is wide and large, and men of valor gather, ten or more, to strike them with whips to produce their sound and to frighten." "<b>The noise of the wheel</b> — the chariot." "<b>And the prancing horse</b> — as in: 'the chargers of his mighty men charge' [Nahum 3:3]."], :book :nahum, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The word טנבו\"ר is transcribed phonetically as it appears; it refers to a type of drum or tambourine."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nahum -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nachum"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:48.189458773Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}